# s7_stream_load: checkpoint streamed tensor by tensor; the whole model is never built.
#
# admission  measured off-path as x4_stream_load; gate byte-identical to s6's
#            (GATE|logits|-1.0620574951e+00 8.0404663086e-01, 11,228,688,384 bytes, 1525 rounds); row reads
#            equivalent because the line is in phase B since s5.
# object     p_census_peak_x2 (97.5% of the per-layer peak): 866.5 MB float32 weights in pairs (49 flat vs
#            49 shaped, 1 vs 1): state_dict and module. Markers: after_model_load 1,150,172 kB, 0.5 s later
#            384,688.
# before     x3 (low_cpu_mem_usage=True): duplicate gone, run worse (median 1,337,108 vs x2's 1,194,020).
# lever      safe_open per scope, encoder layers to disk, posix_fadvise(DONTNEED).
# donor      retired s6_stream_load:
#              s3_disk        1,295,888 kB
#              s4_reduce      1,333,064      a REGRESSION there, contrary to its own summary.md
#              s5_embed_chunk   962,480
#              s6_stream_load   643,784      = 628.7 MiB, the "629 MiB" this repo cites
#            its out-of-process shard split (split_safetensors.py) dropped; model.safetensors read
#            directly, fadvise per scope.
# free       same weights, file and order; sub-models under torch.random.fork_rng().
# expected   ~906,000 kB vs s6's 1,290,000 (-30%); remains above the donor's 643,784 (gap open).
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
